      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-9302",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4",
        "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram",
        "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/4f31b9f180b1b766451685428fc289766832fe5d0c7d8902a601ebf060eab0e7.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}=4\\pi .\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-1)\\cdot 0=-10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-10|\\cdot 4\\pi  \\\\  & =40\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
