        "knowledge_point_id": "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication",
        "problem": "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $2\\times 2$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $AB=BA$\n\nII. $(AB)C=A(BC)$\n\nIII. $A(B-C)=(B-C)A$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $A(B-C)\\ne (B-C)A$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true.",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
